export anchor EditorialGuideStyle:
    number: 2
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Editorial guide
    idea: A printed weekly on warm paper, with serif headlines, ink rules and plain words that read the dashboard like a short report.
    base: light
    palette:
        paper: #faf6ee, the page
        ink: #1f1b16, text, rules, the primary button and this week's chart bars
        graphite: #6b6156, labels, captions and meta text
        hairline: #dcd2c2, thin rules between entries, progress tracks and last week's chart bars
        oxblood: #8c2a1c, links and the Behind status
        forest: #2e5b3a, the On track status
        ochre: #855400, the At risk status
        highlight: #f1eadb, the background of a focused field
    type:
        Serif for headings and body, Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype,
        Palatino, Book Antiqua, Georgia, serif. Labels use the system sans
        in 11px semibold capitals with 0.12em letter spacing. Sizes are a
        44px small-caps wordmark, 40px page headline, 26px section titles,
        22px project names, 17px body at 1.55 line height and 15px italic
        meta. Summary figures are 52px with old-style numerals.
    layout:
        A centred masthead with the wordmark, a date line between ink
        rules, and a centred row of capitalised nav links. A lead section
        pairs the headline and an italic standfirst with four large figures
        split by hairlines. Below it, a two to one column layout holds the
        numbered project entries beside the chart and the activity notes.
        Content is capped at 1180px. Below 640px the columns stack and the
        figures form a two by two grid.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 18px between entries, 32px section padding, 40 to 48px between columns.
    density: Medium. Few elements, long lines and generous leading.
    corners: None. Every edge is square, including buttons.
    borders: A 3px double ink rule under the masthead and above the style sheet, 1px ink under section titles, 1px hairline between entries.
    shadows: None.
    icons:
        No pictogram icons. Status is a capitalised word with a
        typographic symbol, a tick for On track, an open triangle for At
        risk and a cross for Behind. Entries are numbered with italic roman
        numerals. Progress is a thin ink line on a hairline track.
    focus: A 2px ink outline offset 3px. A focused field gets a 2px underline and the highlight background.
    tone: Full sentences, a little formal, such as The week at a glance, Notes from the team and The fortnight. Small numbers are written as words in the activity notes.
